            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0519" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 860c.20/7: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-15T13:00:00-05:00"
                            >January 15, 1919—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 16—3:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>236. Department’s 81, January 3rd reads: “Poles are apparently beginning
                    hostilities against Germans.”</p>
                <p>Does not this reading obviate the inquiry made in your 212, January 9th?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
